\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces Simulated wafer maps under the four disturbance conditions (yellow: failing dies, blue: passing dies). The spatial signatures --- clean, scattered, ring, line --- correspond to the injected disturbances.}}{50}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces Simulated wafer maps under the scaled MSD criterion for three points of the sweep (yellow: failing dies, blue: passing dies). The failing-die population collapses from full-wafer to a single die as the kinematic bounds are relaxed.}}{51}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Synchronization error during one scan under the four control configurations. Shaded band: cruise (exposure) segment.}}{55}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.10}{\ignorespaces Wafer maps across the throughput--yield transition. By 180\,ms the first failures form an eight-die edge cluster at the row-change dies; the cluster persists unchanged through 160\,ms; at 150\,ms the bulk of the wafer has crossed into a \textit {Loc}-classified failure population; by 120\,ms failure is near-total and the map saturates to \textit {Center}.}}{59}{}%
